A multi-wave playbook renders as its verbatim preamble, then the `## Playbook Steps` table with
rows in topological rather than manifest order, then one `## Step:` section per step in the same
order. The preamble's literal Jinja token survives untouched — a non-Jinja playbook body is
inserted, never evaluated — and a healthy graph carries no notice line.

Each section also pins the delegation bullets: `gather` and `draft` are detached by
`<model>:<effort>` and name both model and effort, `named-step` is detached to a named agent,
`plain` is runner-performed and gets the instruction bullets. A detached section carries no
`After:` or `Parallel with:` bullet; `plain`, alone in the last wave, carries `After:` and no
`Parallel with:`. Review gate text is relayed verbatim.

